1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:05,324
Ask an AI a legal question, and it will
give you an answer. Confidently.

2
00:00:05,664 --> 00:00:07,440
But the law changes.

3
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:12,644
This paragraph said a service agreement
had to run at least six months.

4
00:00:12,984 --> 00:00:15,744
Until February, when that floor was
deleted.

5
00:00:16,084 --> 00:00:18,460
So the right answer depends on when you
are asking.

6
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:22,296
Most retrieval systems cannot tell you
which one you got.

7
00:00:22,636 --> 00:00:24,412
This one can.

8
00:00:25,272 --> 00:00:29,904
Warrant is a bitemporal retrieval system
over federal employment regulation.

9
00:00:30,244 --> 00:00:34,793
Every paragraph carries two clocks. When
it was the law, and when the system

10
00:00:34,793 --> 00:00:35,764
believed it was.

11
00:00:36,624 --> 00:00:38,400
Here is what that buys you.

12
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:42,028
How long may a recruitment incentive
service agreement run?

13
00:00:42,368 --> 00:00:48,008
Asked as of June 2024: not less than 6
months, and not more than 4 years.

14
00:00:48,348 --> 00:00:53,361
Asked today: not more than 4 years. Six
words left that paragraph in February, and

15
00:00:53,361 --> 00:00:55,836
the citation says which version it read.

16
00:00:56,696 --> 00:01:02,672
Ask as of 2024, and the gate admits 9,730
paragraphs.

17
00:01:03,012 --> 00:01:06,276
Ask as of today, and it admits 10,007.

18
00:01:06,616 --> 00:01:09,736
Different evidence. Different answer. Both
correct.

19
00:01:10,596 --> 00:01:15,350
The date is not a hint in a prompt. It is
a filter pushed into the query, so

20
00:01:15,350 --> 00:01:18,012
superseded text is never even a candidate.

21
00:01:18,352 --> 00:01:25,096
Removing that filter costs 96 points of
wrong-version rate. 220 wins. 0 losses.

22
00:01:25,956 --> 00:01:28,692
That gate is only as good as what feeds
it.

23
00:01:29,032 --> 00:01:32,800
Five source tiers, from the statute down
to scanned archives.

24
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:38,348
Every snapshot is parsed, stripped of its
apparatus, and diffed against the last one

25
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:39,980
structurally, not by text.

26
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:44,378
What survives is a paragraph with two
clocks on it. That is what the store

27
00:01:44,378 --> 00:01:44,712
holds.

28
00:01:45,572 --> 00:01:48,548
A question then walks the same path every
time.

29
00:01:48,888 --> 00:01:54,852
The date and the scope become predicates,
so the store hands back 9,627 candidates

30
00:01:54,852 --> 00:01:56,472
instead of everything.

31
00:01:56,812 --> 00:02:02,251
Lexical and dense retrieval run
concurrently — 14 and 15 ms — fused by

32
00:02:02,251 --> 00:02:04,300
rank rather than by score.

33
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:10,095
Then generation emits claims with evidence
ids, an aligner computes the spans, and

34
00:02:10,095 --> 00:02:13,328
the whole run is written down under one
trace id.

35
00:02:14,188 --> 00:02:17,356
And when it is wrong, every stage recorded
what it saw.

36
00:02:17,696 --> 00:02:22,815
So the question is not, why did the model
hallucinate. It is, which stage lost the

37
00:02:22,815 --> 00:02:23,384
evidence.

38
00:02:24,244 --> 00:02:27,076
None of that is worth anything unless it
is measured.

39
00:02:27,416 --> 00:02:32,186
Four buckets. Three mined automatically
from amendment diffs, and one written by

40
00:02:32,186 --> 00:02:35,024
hand, which is the one that measures
usefulness.

41
00:02:35,364 --> 00:02:40,621
That hand-written set went from 29 items
to 212. The score barely moved. The

42
00:02:40,621 --> 00:02:42,444
interval more than halved.

43
00:02:42,784 --> 00:02:45,976
The old number was not wrong. It was
unfalsifiable.

44
00:02:46,836 --> 00:02:49,236
In production the same discipline applies.

45
00:02:49,576 --> 00:02:55,389
Metrics for every stage, and logs carrying
two ids. One groups a call. One names a

46
00:02:55,389 --> 00:02:56,824
replayable artifact.

47
00:02:57,164 --> 00:03:01,486
A request refused at the door has the
first and not the second, which separates

48
00:03:01,486 --> 00:03:03,980
answering wrongly from never answering at
all.

49
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:09,145
And a build fails on regression against a
bootstrapped lower bound, because a gate

50
00:03:09,145 --> 00:03:12,600
set at the point estimate fails half of
all unchanged runs.

51
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:15,884
Five components in here ship switched off.

52
00:03:16,224 --> 00:03:21,372
A reranker. An entailment verifier. A
calibrated confidence model. Multi-hop

53
00:03:21,372 --> 00:03:23,568
retrieval. A fine-tuned encoder.

54
00:03:23,908 --> 00:03:28,269
Each one built. Each one measured. Each
one disabled, with the p-value that

55
00:03:28,269 --> 00:03:30,508
decided it sitting next to the switch.

56
00:03:31,368 --> 00:03:35,232
Because measuring something and shipping
it anyway is not engineering.

57
00:03:35,572 --> 00:03:40,372
Warrant. The code, and every measurement,
including the ones that came out negative.
